Z||000000||Notchit||12-28-2000||02:26 AM||||Alright, i bought a 1985 Fiero GT, automatic V6 with 82,000 Km on it this summer, its been in my garage since. I was told by the guy i bought it from that there was a small problem with the engine, when you rev it to 2500 rpm (in park) it makes a click click click sound, not too loud, but enough to hear it inside the car...he told me it was most likely a stuck lifter. I would like to hear your imput on this!<P>thanks <P><P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR>_________________________||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||12-28-2000||02:46 PM||||My first guess would be an exhaust leak.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||12-28-2000||03:00 PM||||I'd go with cracked exhaust manifold.<P>Could be a stick injector too.<BR>I think<P>Try listening to the engine and revving it up to see if you can detremine where the noise is coming from.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Notchit||12-28-2000||03:47 PM||||Well i just started it up, its more like a rattle then anything, at that RPM....i can't hear it at any other....||||reg||4
Z||000004||mshill||12-28-2000||05:39 PM||||Check the springs that connect the exhaust system to the cradle.  If a spring is hanging it will rattle around at specific RPMs.  Usually the exhaust leak would be evident at all RPMs including idle, but definitely worse at higher RPM and even worse under load.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Notchit||12-28-2000||05:52 PM||||Nope....no spring that I can see.....I think i'll just get a mechanic to take a gander at it, if it was an exhaust leak, how loud would it be?||||reg||6
Z||000006||StuGood||12-28-2000||06:04 PM||||You might want to try the stethoscope trick first.  Put one end of a length of hose to your ear.  Move the the other end of the hose around the (running) engine, near possible sources of the click.  When you find the source of the noise, you'll hear it very distinctly.<P>Don't forget to try the forward exhaust manifold.  That's not where you want the problem, but it's a fairly common exhaust leak.  Also investigate the sheet metal heat shield on the forward firewall.   ||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||12-28-2000||08:24 PM||||The exhaust typical fiero manifold exhaust leak sounds like a lifter noise and is about as loud as one too. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||80's BOY||12-28-2000||08:45 PM||||loose rocker arm maybe?? see if it gets faster with different RPM's. increase/decrease in ticking noise etc.||||reg||1
Z||000009||KnightRyder31||12-28-2000||10:01 PM||||You know, I have this same problem...and its bothering me!!!<BR>It's not constant, it only comes when it wants to. It gets pretty loud also, and seems to come when the engine is warmed up. <BR>It really makes me mad too! At times I can hear it over my radio, and I listen to my music very loud. I really need help with this. Its a ticking noise, not clicking. <BR>I've heard that it was lifter's, push arms or rods, valve problem, rod knock, ect. Nobody can give me a straight answer.<BR>My fiero is a 84 coupe with 73, XXX miles on her. She also has a crappy idle...and poor gas mileage.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Notchit||12-29-2000||12:42 AM||||yeah, i have low km's as well, and it makes me a bit mad, unfortunatly i'm 17....so i've been looking at parts (such as manifold) to distinguish them from others....and it does go faster (the click/rattle noise)  when I give it a little more gas, then after about 3200 rpm it goes away.....very confused and frustrated. (but i still love my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR>_________________________||||reg||1
